Suggested approach for Implement a secure webhook endpoint:
1. Implement the requirement in the named App Router convention or trusted server layer.
2. Add explicit input validation and a user-friendly empty/error/denied state.
3. Exercise the normal case and at least one boundary case.
4. Run lint/tests and a production build in the target Next.js version.

Starter to adapt:
export async function POST(request) {
  const signature = request.headers.get('x-provider-signature');
  if (!signature || !verifySignature(signature, await request.text())) return new Response('Invalid signature', { status: 401 });
  return Response.json({ received: true });
}

Required static markers: x-provider-signature, verifySignature, status: 401. These only provide a limited automatic signal; acceptance criteria must be manually reviewed.
